WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Speaker 1: I talked about this next story&nbsp;
on last Friday's bonus show, but it's just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.680
such an important media story. I thought it'd&nbsp;
be good to cover again today for the general&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.680
David Pakman show audience, and that is that as I&nbsp;
was watching day one of the January 6th hearings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.480
last Thursday, I couldn't help but wonder,&nbsp;
is Fox News broadcasting this? Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.320
on the one hand, it's a highly relevant thing&nbsp;
that's going on in the world of politics. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.960
you'd think that a news and politics TV station&nbsp;
would have to cover it. On the other hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.080
the January six hearings are really making Trump&nbsp;
look bad, really making his allies look bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.480
and even making Fox News personalities look&nbsp;
bad. Because, you know, we found out about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.040
how Sean HANNITY was texting Kayleigh MCENANY&nbsp;
as the Capitol riots were unfolding, trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.880
get her to get the president to get his supporters&nbsp;
out of the Capitol on that day. Well, what I saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:53.360
was Tucker Carlson show, and they had a live feed&nbsp;
up of the hearing, but they weren't playing audio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:58.640
from it. They were just showing the visuals. And&nbsp;
Tucker went on the show and he brought on guests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.520
and he was complaining about how the whole ordeal&nbsp;
was overblown and how we're not talking about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.440
real issues because we're so wrapped up at January&nbsp;
6th. Still, Carlson called the hearing deranged.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:15.280
He called it insulting, and he took a moral stand.&nbsp;
He said that he was going to simply refuse to play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.320
along the lower third graphics during the show.&nbsp;
That's the sirens at the bottom. They were saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:26.160
things like January 6th committee fuels false&nbsp;
narratives as sham investigation draws on. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.840
was another one that said leaders will spend 90&nbsp;
minutes giving moral lecture. A third one said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.240
Our leaders are focusing on January 6th&nbsp;
while ignoring the real threats. Here's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.800
clip from Tucker Carlson's opening monologue.
Speaker 2: Good evening and welcome to Tucker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.640
Carlson. You know, it tells you a lot about the&nbsp;
priorities of our ruling class that the rest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:50.800
us are getting yet. Another lecture about January&nbsp;
six tonight from our moral inferiors, no less,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.240
an outbreak of mob violence, a forgettable&nbsp;
minor outbreak by recent standards that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.440
took place more than a year and a half ago,&nbsp;
but they've never stopped talking about it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:06.400
In the meantime, in the 18 months since January&nbsp;
six, gas prices have doubled. Drug loads have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.960
reached their highest point ever. The U.S. economy&nbsp;
is now careening toward a devastating recession&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:17.360
at best. And scariest and least noted of all,&nbsp;
this country has never in its history been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:22.800
closer to a nuclear war. Yet the other networks&nbsp;
cannot be bothered to cover any of that tonight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.360
Instead, they've interrupted the regularly&nbsp;
scheduled programing to bring you yet another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.880
extended primetime harangue from Nancy Pelosi&nbsp;
and Liz Cheney about Donald Trump and Q and on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.800
The whole thing is insulting. In fact,&nbsp;
it's deranged and we're not playing along.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:44.400
This is the only hour on an American news channel&nbsp;
that will not be carrying their propaganda live.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.120
They are lying and we are not going to help&nbsp;
them do it. What we will do instead is to try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.880
to tell you the truth. We've attempted&nbsp;
to do that since the day this happened.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.120
We hated seeing vandalism at the US Capitol a&nbsp;
year and a half ago and we said so at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.480
but we did not think it was an insurrection&nbsp;
because it was not an insurrection. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.320
was not even close to an insurrection.
Speaker 1: Now, it's also interesting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.800
all of this is that during the entire broadcast,&nbsp;
they didn't actually cut to a commercial break.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.320
And you have to wonder why that is, right? Because&nbsp;
it's a TV show. Like any other show. You're going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.000
to go to commercials every 15 minutes to&nbsp;
give time for the sponsors. Well, what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.200
appears to have happened is that Fox executives&nbsp;
didn't want people to have the opportunity to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.680
change the channel. Right. Because if they go to&nbsp;
break at Fox, maybe people will tune over to CNN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.560
or another news station, and then maybe they'll&nbsp;
come across the hearings with the audio and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.720
they may actually learn a thing or two about&nbsp;
January 6th. So couldn't have that, which meant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.200
that you couldn't have commercials. And that's&nbsp;
really telling, right? Because on the one hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.160
Fox is saying that January 6th there was nothing.&nbsp;
BERGER There's too much focus on it. It was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:51.520
a tourist visit, nothing to see here. And on the&nbsp;
other hand, they're unwilling to go to commercial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.960
breaks. They're unwilling to broadcast the hearing&nbsp;
with audio. So they definitely have something to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.160
hide when it comes to all of this. And they want&nbsp;
to make sure that their viewers don't learn too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.120
much more about the events of January 6th and the&nbsp;
lead up. Now, I'm sure we'll be talking more about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:10.880
the hearings as they continue this week. But to&nbsp;
be honest, from day one of the hearings, I had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:15.520
mixed feelings because I thought that the video&nbsp;
