00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:20.480
the footage of the riots and, you know, the Trump&nbsp;
supporters who are fighting with the cops and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.120
that stuff, I thought it was very effective. What&nbsp;
I didn't think was so effective was some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:31.360
long winded speeches and the testimony from the&nbsp;
police officer and the documentarian and the focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.040
on the proud boys and all that stuff. I think&nbsp;
if it was a little bit more condensed, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:40.400
be more effective, but that's just my view anyway.&nbsp;
You're trying to appeal to people who haven't made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.960
up their minds when it comes to January 6th, and&nbsp;
I think less is more when it comes to this stuff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:51.440
So we'll we'll see what happens over the next few&nbsp;
days as the hearings continue. If they are able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:57.040
to engage with the audience any better and if the&nbsp;
public is able to come away from this all thinking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:01.360
that there really needs to be consequences for&nbsp;
the people who were involved on January 6th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.840
because it was a terrible thing that happens in&nbsp;
our country and it should never happen again.

